%U A402099 224362872,238324224,242813184,242986240,253800864,288194816,4265699760,5130177120,6082519392
%N A402099 Numbers k such that psi(k) = phi(k) + Omega(k)^8.
%C A402099 The Python program available in the linked GitHub repository computes the solutions to the equation psi(k) = phi(k) + Omega(k)^m for arbitrary positive integer values of m. For this sequence, use m = 8.
%H A402099 S. I. Dimitrov, <a href="https://github.com/Stoyan16/Numbers-k-such-that-psi-k-phi-k-Omega-k-6/blob/main/A401783">Python program</a> (GitHub).
%e A402099 2071 is a term since psi(2071) = 2200 = 1944 + 2^8 = phi(2071) + Omega(2071)^8.
%o A402099 (PARI) isok(k) = {my(f = factor(k)); prod(i=1, #f~, (f[i, 1]+1) * f[i, 1]^(f[i, 2]-1)) - eulerphi(f) == bigomega(f)^8; } \\ _Amiram Eldar_, Nov 16 2026
%Y A402099 Cf. A000010, A001222, A001615, A401783, A402098.
%K A402099 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A402099 1,2
